 # todo
 
-A small CLI todo manager backed by a JSON file. `python -m todo.cli --file t.json add "x"`.
+A small CLI todo manager. By default it stores tasks in a SQLite database at `~/.todo.db`; a JSON file backend is still available by using a path that ends with `.json` (e.g. `--file t.json`). The storage path can also be set with the `TODO_FILE` environment variable.
+
+```bash
+python -m todo.cli add "ship release"          # uses ~/.todo.db
+python -m todo.cli --file t.json add "x"       # JSON backend
+python -m todo.cli rename 1 "new title"        # rename a task
+python -m todo.cli migrate old.json new.db     # copy tasks between backends
+```
+
+`migrate SRC DST` copies all tasks from one store to the other (either direction, chosen by file extension), preserving ids, done flags, timestamps and tags. The destination must be empty, otherwise it fails with `destination not empty`.
+
 Tests: `python -m pytest -q`.
